<PageTitle>@GlobalValues.Component_Name_GoTo @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Api</PageTitle>

<h1>@GlobalValues.Component_Name_GoTo @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Api . . . In Progress . . .</h1>

<GoTo LabelText="GoTo API page title" />

<p>
    Everything you need to work with the GoTo component: parameters, methods, and CSS variables for styling.
</p>







<section>
    <h2 class="mobile-centred-heading">Component parameters.</h2>
    <p>
        The following sections cover the two components, the <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">GoTo</span> marker and the <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">GoToViewer</span>, including their parameters.
        Neither component exposes public methods for you to call.
    </p>

    <section>
        <h3 id="goto-component-parameters" class="mobile-centred-heading">GoTo component parameters</h3>
        <div class="@Section.Base @Section.NoPadding @Section.OverflowX(UnitScroll.Auto) @Padding.Block(UnitSpace.Four)">
            <table class="@Table.Base @Table.CodeTable" tabindex="0" aria-labelledby="goto-component-parameters">
                <thead>
                    <tr>
                        <th scope="col">Parameter</th>
                        <th scope="col">Type</th>
                        <th scope="col">Description</th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr>
                        <td>LabelText</td>
                        <td>string</td>
                        <td>
                            Gets or sets the text shown for the marker in the viewer's list and in the label displayed when the marker is reached. Leading and trailing whitespace is trimmed.
                            Required - an <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">ArgumentNullException</span> is thrown if it is <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">null</span>, empty or whitespace.
                        </td>
                    </tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h3 id="goto-viewer-component-parameters" class="mobile-centred-heading">GoToViewer component parameters</h3>
        <div class="@Section.Base @Section.NoPadding @Section.OverflowX(UnitScroll.Auto) @Padding.Block(UnitSpace.Four)">
            <table class="@Table.Base @Table.CodeTable" tabindex="0" aria-labelledby="goto-viewer-component-parameters">
                <thead>
                    <tr>
                        <th scope="col">Parameter</th>
                        <th scope="col">Type</th>
                        <th scope="col">Description</th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr>
                        <td>HeadingText</td>
                        <td>string</td>
                        <td>
                            Gets or sets the heading of the viewer, which is also its accessible name. Leading and trailing whitespace is trimmed. If <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">null</span>, empty or whitespace,
                            the default is used. Defaults to "Go to Markers".
                        </td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td>CloseButtonText</td>
                        <td>string</td>
                        <td>
                            Gets or sets the text of the viewer's close button. Leading and trailing whitespace is trimmed. If <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">null</span>, empty or whitespace,
                            the default is used. Defaults to "Close".
                        </td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td>NoGotoMarkersText</td>
                        <td>string</td>
                        <td>
                            Gets or sets the message shown in the viewer when the page has no markers. Leading and trailing whitespace is trimmed. If <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">null</span>, empty or whitespace,
                            the default is used. Defaults to "No go to markers defined for this page.".
                        </td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td>TriggerButtonText</td>
                        <td>string</td>
                        <td>
                            Gets or sets the text of the trigger button, which stays hidden until it receives keyboard focus. It should mention the keyboard shortcut. Leading and trailing whitespace is trimmed.
                            If <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">null</span>, empty or whitespace, the default is used. Defaults to "Go to viewer (Control + Shift + Y)".
                        </td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td>ExcludeTriggerButton</td>
                        <td>bool</td>
                        <td>
                            Gets or sets whether the trigger button is left out. When <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">true</span>, the viewer can only be opened with the keyboard shortcut.
                            Defaults to <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">false</span>.
                        </td>
                    </tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
    </section>
</section>

<section>
    <h2 class="mobile-centred-heading">CSS variables defined for the GoTo components.</h2>

    <p>
        The following sections outline all of the CSS variables that can be set to alter the styling of the viewer, its trigger button and the numbered badges.
        You can of course also override the style classes directly.
    </p>

    <section>
        <h3 id="goto-behaviour-variables" class="mobile-centred-heading">Scroll offset and badge variables</h3>
        <div class="@Section.Base @Section.NoPadding @Section.OverflowX(UnitScroll.Auto) @Padding.Block(UnitSpace.Four)">
            <table class="@Table.Base @Table.CodeTable" tabindex="0" aria-labelledby="goto-behaviour-variables">
                <thead>
                    <tr>
                        <th scope="col">Variable Name</th>
                        <th scope="col">Default Value</th>
                        <th scope="col">Description</th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr>
                        <td>--br-comp-goto-scroll-offset</td>
                        <td>4rem</td>
                        <td>
                            The space kept above a marker when it is scrolled into view, so that a fixed header is less likely to cover it. Set it to the height of your fixed header.
                            If your site already sets <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">scroll-padding</span> for the same header, the two values combine, so use one or the other.
                        </td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td>--br-comp-goto-badge-size</td>
                        <td>3rem</td>
                        <td>The width and height of the numbered badge shown beside each marker while the viewer is open. The badge is always a circle.</td>
                    </tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
    </section>

